<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xuanzheng Yuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1264">1264</a>–<a href="/years/1368">1368</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Bureau of Buddhist and Tibetan Affairs, Zongzhi Yuan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xuanzheng Yuan, or Bureau of Buddhist and Tibetan Affairs, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> office that administered Buddhist clergy and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>. Founded as the Zongzhi Yuan in 1264 under the Imperial Preceptor Phagpa and renamed in 1288, it worked through the Sakya hierarchs, who ruled Tibet as regional authorities under Mongol patronage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xuanzheng-yuan.jpg" alt="Xuanzheng Yuan" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jason22 and Chinyin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yuan_dynasty_and_Tibet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
